The `reverse` method takes a string `word` as input and returns a string containing the same word with the characters reversed. It uses a `StringBuilder` object to reverse the characters.

For example, if the input string is "Mr Ding", the function will return "rM gniD".

public static String reverseWords(String s) {
    String[] words = s.split(" ");
    for (int i = 0; i < words.length; i++) {
        char[] chars = words[i].toCharArray();
        for (int j = 0; j < chars.length / 2; j++) {
            char temp = chars[j];
            chars[j] = chars[chars.length - j - 1];
            chars[chars.length - j - 1] = temp;
        }
        words[i] = new String(chars);
    }
    return String.join(" ", words);
}

